{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba p1a/witnesses/w1-fixture.c; nl -ba p1a/witnesses/w1-errno.scm | sed -n '1,265p'; nl -ba /Users/sto/.local/share/mise/plugins/gambit/lib/utils.bash | sed -n '55,76p'; cat /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/AGENTS.md\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t/* W1 fixture — errno-atomicity call shapes.\n     2\t *\n     3\t * Each w1_*_ptr function is the \"typed C shim\" of the jolt contract: it\n     4\t * performs a target \"call\" and captures (result, errno) IMMEDIATELY after the\n     5\t * target returns, before any cleanup or re-entry (the astra essential\n     6\t * sequence). A deliberate post-capture clobber (errno = 7777) inside the shim\n     7\t * proves the capture order: the Scheme side must see the captured value, not\n     8\t * the clobbered one.\n     9\t *\n    10\t * The pair travels out of the shim as one malloc'd struct, so the Scheme side\n    11\t * reads result and errno from a single allocation — no second read of errno\n    12\t * can intervene. A global \"last errno\" cell would fail the interleaved and\n    13\t * threaded iterations; re-reading errno after any cleanup would fail the\n    14\t * post-capture clobber.\n    15\t */\n    16\t\n    17\t#include <errno.h>\n    18\t#include <stdlib.h>\n    19\t#include <stdio.h>\n    20\t\n    21\t/* c-define'd in w1-errno.scm */\n    22\textern int w1_nested_cb (int x);\n    23\t\n    24\ttypedef struct { int res; int err; } w1_pair;\n    25\t\n    26\tstatic int w1_target_a (void) { errno = 0; return -1; }   /* caller maps to EAGAIN */\n    27\tstatic int w1_target_b (void) { return 7; }               /* success, errno 42 preserved */\n    28\tstatic int w1_target_c (void) { errno = 0; return -2; }   /* caller maps to EACCES */\n    29\t\n    30\t/* shape A: failure with EAGAIN */\n    31\tw1_pair *w1_shape_a (void)\n    32\t{\n    33\t  int r;\n    34\t  w1_pair *p;\n    35\t  errno = 0;\n    36\t  r = w1_target_a ();\n    37\t  if (r < 0) errno = EAGAIN;\n    38\t  p = malloc (sizeof (w1_pair));\n    39\t  p->res = r;\n    40\t  p->err = errno;      /* capture immediately after target */\n    41\t  errno = 7777;        /* deliberate post-capture clobber */\n    42\t  return p;\n    43\t}\n    44\t\n    45\t/* shape B: success that PRESERVES errno = 42 (contract: do not normalize\n    46\t   success to zero) */\n    47\tw1_pair *w1_shape_b (void)\n    48\t{\n    49\t  int r;\n    50\t  w1_pair *p;\n    51\t  errno = 42;\n    52\t  r = w1_target_b ();\n    53\t  p = malloc (sizeof (w1_pair));\n    54\t  p->res = r;\n    55\t  p->err = errno;      /* capture immediately, success included */\n    56\t  errno = 7777;\n    57\t  return p;\n    58\t}\n    59\t\n    60\t/* shape C: failure with EACCES */\n    61\tw1_pair *w1_shape_c (void)\n    62\t{\n    63\t  int r;\n    64\t  w1_pair *p;\n    65\t  errno = 0;\n    66\t  r = w1_target_c ();\n    67\t  if (r < 0) errno = EACCES;\n    68\t  p = malloc (sizeof (w1_pair));\n    69\t  p->res = r;\n    70\t  p->err = errno;\n    71\t  errno = 7777;\n    72\t  return p;\n    73\t}\n    74\t\n    75\t/* shape D: like C, but the c-lambda body adds an ___AT_END clobber that runs\n    76\t   AFTER the result conversion — the captured pair must not change. */\n    77\t\n    78\t/* shape E: nested calls. Captures EIO first, then re-enters Scheme via the\n    79\t   c-define'd callback w1_nested_cb (which itself performs a nested foreign\n    80\t   call and clobbers errno through its own shim), then returns the pair\n    81\t   captured BEFORE the re-entry. A shim that re-read errno after the nested\n    82\t   call would show the callback's post-clobber value instead of EIO. */\n    83\tw1_pair *w1_shape_e (void)\n    84\t{\n    85\t  w1_pair *p;\n    86\t  int cb;\n    87\t  errno = EIO;\n    88\t  p = malloc (sizeof (w1_pair));\n    89\t  p->res = -3;\n    90\t  p->err = errno;      /* capture immediately */\n    91\t  cb = w1_nested_cb (5);   /* re-enter Scheme; inner shim B runs inside */\n    92\t  if (cb != 12)        /* callback sanity: must return exactly 12 */\n    93\t    {\n    94\t      p->res = -999;\n    95\t      p->err = cb;\n    96\t    }\n    97\t  errno = 7777;        /* deliberate post-capture clobber */\n    98\t  return p;\n    99\t}\n   100\t\n   101\tvoid w1_free_pair (w1_pair *p) { free (p); }\n   102\t\n   103\t/* Platform errno values probed by the Scheme side so the assertions hold on\n   104\t   any OS (EAGAIN/EACCES/EIO differ between macOS and Linux). */\n   105\tint w1_errno_again (void) { return EAGAIN; }\n   106\tint w1_errno_acces (void) { return EACCES; }\n   107\tint w1_errno_io    (void) { return EIO; }\n     1\t;; W1 — errno-atomicity witness (astra's \"essential sequence\").\n     2\t;;\n     3\t;; Asserts the Scheme side sees the right (result, errno) pair EVERY time for:\n     4\t;;   - shape A (-1, EAGAIN), shape B (7, 42 preserved on success), shape C (-2, EACCES)\n     5\t;;   - shape D: c-lambda code body with a deliberate ___AT_END clobber AFTER\n     6\t;;     the result conversion (capture order proof at the conversion boundary)\n     7\t;;   - shape E: capture before a nested re-entry into Scheme (per-invocation\n     8\t;;     capture, not a global \"last errno\" cell), including the documented\n     9\t;;     C->Scheme->C->Scheme nesting on one thread (manual §\"Continuations,\n    10\t;;     the C-interface and threads\")\n    11\t;;   - concurrent calls from two Scheme threads with interleaved shapes\n    12\t;;\n    13\t;; Run: ./w1.exe\n    14\t\n    15\t(c-declare #<<c-declare-end\n    16\t\n    17\t#include <errno.h>\n    18\t\n    19\ttypedef struct { int res; int err; } w1_pair;\n    20\t\n    21\tw1_pair *w1_shape_a (void);\n    22\tw1_pair *w1_shape_b (void);\n    23\tw1_pair *w1_shape_c (void);\n    24\tw1_pair *w1_shape_e (void);\n    25\tvoid w1_free_pair (w1_pair *p);\n    26\tint w1_errno_again (void);\n    27\tint w1_errno_acces (void);\n    28\tint w1_errno_io (void);\n    29\t\n    30\tc-declare-end\n    31\t)\n    32\t\n    33\t(c-define-type w1-pair (pointer \"w1_pair\"))\n    34\t\n    35\t;; platform errno values (EAGAIN/EACCES/EIO differ between macOS and Linux)\n    36\t(define w1-EAGAIN ((c-lambda () int \"w1_errno_again\")))\n    37\t(define w1-EACCES ((c-lambda () int \"w1_errno_acces\")))\n    38\t(define w1-EIO    ((c-lambda () int \"w1_errno_io\")))\n    39\t\n    40\t(define w1-call-a (c-lambda () w1-pair \"w1_shape_a\"))\n    41\t(define w1-call-b (c-lambda () w1-pair \"w1_shape_b\"))\n    42\t(define w1-call-c (c-lambda () w1-pair \"w1_shape_c\"))\n    43\t(define w1-call-e (c-lambda () w1-pair \"w1_shape_e\"))\n    44\t\n    45\t;; shape D: c-lambda code body, ___AT_END clobber after result conversion.\n    46\t(define w1-call-d\n    47\t  (c-lambda () w1-pair\n    48\t#<<c-lambda-end\n    49\t   w1_pair *p = w1_shape_c ();\n    50\t   ___return (p);\n    51\t   #define ___AT_END errno = 31337;\n    52\tc-lambda-end\n    53\t))\n    54\t\n    55\t(define w1-pair-res (c-lambda (w1-pair) int \"___return (___arg1->res);\"))\n    56\t(define w1-pair-err (c-lambda (w1-pair) int \"___return (___arg1->err);\"))\n    57\t(define w1-free-pair (c-lambda (w1-pair) void \"w1_free_pair (___arg1); ___return;\"))\n    58\t\n    59\t;; c-define'd callback used by shape E: performs a nested foreign call\n    60\t;; (shape B) and returns exactly 12 when x = 5.\n    61\t(c-define (w1-nested-cb x) (int) int \"w1_nested_cb\" \"extern\"\n    62\t  (if (= x 5)\n    63\t      (let ((p (w1-call-b)))\n    64\t        (let ((r (+ (w1-pair-res p) (w1-pair-err p))))  ; 7 + 42, forces both reads\n    65\t          (w1-free-pair p)\n    66\t          (if (= r 49) 12 r)))\n    67\t      -1))\n    68\t\n    69\t(define w1-failures 0)\n    70\t(define w1-checks 0)\n    71\t\n    72\t(define (w1-check! tag p er es)\n    73\t  (set! w1-checks (+ w1-checks 1))\n    74\t  (let ((r (w1-pair-res p)) (e (w1-pair-err p)))\n    75\t    (if (not (and (= r er) (= e es)))\n    76\t        (begin\n    77\t          (set! w1-failures (+ w1-failures 1))\n    78\t          (display \"W1-MISMATCH: \") (display tag)\n    79\t          (display \" got (\") (display r) (display \",\") (display e)\n    80\t          (display \") expected (\") (display er) (display \",\") (display es)\n    81\t          (display \")\")\n    82\t          (newline)))\n    83\t    (w1-free-pair p)))\n    84\t\n    85\t(define (w1-loop! tag call er es n)\n    86\t  (let loop ((i 0))\n    87\t    (if (< i n)\n    88\t        (begin\n    89\t          (w1-check! tag (call) er es)\n    90\t          (loop (+ i 1))))))\n    91\t\n    92\t(define (w1-worker tid)\n    93\t  ;; interleaved shapes from one thread; a global \"last errno\" cell cannot\n    94\t  ;; survive this interleave, per-invocation capture must.\n    95\t  (let loop ((i 0))\n    96\t    (if (< i 400)\n    97\t        (begin\n    98\t          (w1-check! \"A\" (w1-call-a) -1 w1-EAGAIN)\n    99\t          (w1-check! \"B\" (w1-call-b) 7 42)\n   100\t          (w1-check! \"C\" (w1-call-c) -2 w1-EACCES)\n   101\t          (w1-check! \"E\" (w1-call-e) -3 w1-EIO)\n   102\t          (thread-sleep! 0.0001)              ; force green interleaving\n   103\t          (loop (+ i 1))))))\n   104\t\n   105\t(display \"=== W1 errno-atomicity witness ===\")\n   106\t(newline)\n   107\t(display \"EAGAIN=\") (display w1-EAGAIN) (display \" EACCES=\") (display w1-EACCES)\n   108\t(display \" EIO=\") (display w1-EIO) (newline)\n   109\t(set! w1-failures 0)\n   110\t(set! w1-checks 0)\n   111\t\n   112\t;; sequential shapes\n   113\t(w1-loop! \"A\" w1-call-a -1 w1-EAGAIN 200)\n   114\t(w1-loop! \"B\" w1-call-b 7 42 200)\n   115\t(w1-loop! \"C\" w1-call-c -2 w1-EACCES 200)\n   116\t(w1-loop! \"D\" w1-call-d -2 w1-EACCES 100)      ; ___AT_END clobber must not leak\n   117\t(w1-loop! \"E\" w1-call-e -3 w1-EIO 100)         ; nested re-entry capture\n   118\t\n   119\t;; concurrent shapes from two Scheme threads\n   120\t(define t1 (make-thread (lambda () (w1-worker 1)) 'w1-t1))\n   121\t(define t2 (make-thread (lambda () (w1-worker 2)) 'w1-t2))\n   122\t(thread-start! t1)\n   123\t(thread-start! t2)\n   124\t(thread-join! t1)\n   125\t(thread-join! t2)\n   126\t\n   127\t(display \"W1-CHECKS=\") (display w1-checks) (newline)\n   128\t(display \"W1-FAILURES=\") (display w1-failures) (newline)\n   129\t(if (= w1-failures 0)\n   130\t    (display \"W1-VERDICT: PASS (result+errno pair captured atomically at the shim; capture order proven by post-capture and ___AT_END clobbers; per-invocation capture proven by nesting and threads)\")\n   131\t    (display \"W1-VERDICT: FAIL\"))\n   132\t(newline)\n    55\t\n    56\t\tif [ \"$install_type\" != \"version\" ]; then\n    57\t\t\tfail \"asdf-$TOOL_NAME supports release installs only\"\n    58\t\tfi\n    59\t\n    60\t\t(\n    61\t\t\tmake() {\n    62\t\t\t\tcommand make -j\"$(getconf _NPROCESSORS_ONLN)\" \"$@\"\n    63\t\t\t}\n    64\t\n    65\t\t\tmkdir -p \"$install_path\"\n    66\t\n    67\t\t\tcd \"$ASDF_DOWNLOAD_PATH\"\n    68\t\t\t./configure --enable-single-host --prefix=\"${install_path}\"\n    69\t\t\tmake check\n    70\t\t\tmake install\n    71\t\n    72\t\t\t# TODO: Assert gambit executable exists.\n    73\t\t\tlocal tool_cmd\n    74\t\t\ttool_cmd=\"$(echo \"$TOOL_TEST\" | cut -d' ' -f1)\"\n    75\t\t\ttest -x \"$install_path/bin/$tool_cmd\" || fail \"Expected $install_path/bin/$tool_cmd to be executable.\"\n    76\t\n# ==============================================================================\n# datom.world – Development Rules & Architectural Foundations\n# ==============================================================================\n\nSee [`docs/design/datom.world.md`](./docs/design/datom.world.md) for master architecture, core philosophy, foundational axioms, non-negotiable invariants, code style, development workflow, and operational guides (testing, team roles, agent delegation, website formats).\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"agent_message","text":"The main results reproduce, with one mismatch: `w3-phase2-run2.out` records exit 70, while my rerun segfaulted with exit 139. Both are consistent with unsafe entry. I also found a substantive W1 defect: the shims call `malloc` before saving errno, so 4000 passing checks do not prove astra’s required capture-before-allocation sequence."}}
