ility remains unsupported. Any probe that actually invokes subprocess creation inside the target requires that capability or remains explicitly unqualified.\n   250\t\n   251\t**Corpus acceptance means identical semantic results and refusal behavior, not identical timing.** Preserve platform-specific applicability and mark missing legs PARTIAL. Do not label a partial corpus pass as Gambit parity.\n   252\t\n   253\t**5. Effort and P1 decision**\n   254\t\n   255\tThese estimates include implementation, fixtures, platform qualification, patch packaging, and review. The approximately 11,000-line adapter is the reference unit; generated seeds and vendored dependencies are excluded.\n   256\t\n   257\t| Slice | Relative effort | Indicative engineering time |\n   258\t|---|---:|---:|\n   259\t| P1 runtime audit and decisive witnesses | 0.10–0.20 adapter units | 3–5 days |\n   260\t| P1 bridge, compiler/boot integration, gates, patch tooling | 0.45–0.80 | 3–6 weeks |\n   261\t| P2 crypto qualification | 0.10–0.20 | 1–2 weeks |\n   262\t| P3 file plus parser qualification | 0.25–0.45 | 2–4 weeks |\n   263\t| General runtime signatures, unrestricted callbacks, or AOT beyond the bounded tier | Additional 0.30–0.70 | Separate estimate after P1 |\n   264\t\n   265\tThese are engineering-effort estimates, not a prediction of generated line count. Runtime changes could exceed the upper range; they require a new decision rather than being absorbed silently into P1.\n   266\t\n   267\t**GO after P1** requires:\n   268\t\n   269\t- Exact runtime mechanisms and configuration recorded from 4.9.8 source.\n   270\t- Both pinned rows demonstrated on both target platforms.\n   271\t- Target-identified public jolt execution, not only standalone C/Scheme fixtures.\n   272\t- Qualified callable modes and explicit refusals for every remaining mode.\n   273\t- No moving-memory exposure across released calls.\n   274\t- Reproducible patch application, seeds, negative gates, and rollback.\n   275\t- Existing Gambit and relevant Chez gates preserved.\n   276\t\n   277\t**Partial GO:** memory, loading, ordinary calls, and errno may land independently when qualified. Retain blocking/callback refusals and describe the result as partial FFI. This does **not** authorize P2/P3 parity claims.\n   278\t\n   279\t**NO-GO for P2/P3:** collection cannot complete while C is blocked; unrelated C-thread entry cannot be made safe where required; exact runtime ownership rules remain unknown; or the solution depends on silently moving generic calls to another native thread.\n   280\t\n   281\tIf 4.9.8 cannot meet the necessary runtime transitions, the next decision is an explicit Gambit upgrade or runtime patch through the upgrade gate. The fallback remains honest refusal, with Chez retaining the affected capability.\n   282\t\n   283\tDONE\n    80\t                             (w4-log \"W4-M3: thread B attempting callback t=\" (w4-now))\n    81\t                             (let ((r (w4-m3-b)))\n    82\t                               (w4-m3-note 1)\n    83\t                               (w4-log \"W4-M3: thread B callback completed t=\" (w4-now)\n    84\t                                       \" -> \" r)\n    85\t                               r))\n    86\t                           'w4-b)))\n    87\t    (thread-start! t-a)\n    88\t    (thread-start! t-b)\n    89\t    (let ((t-start (w4-now)))\n    90\t      (thread-join! t-a)\n    91\t      (let ((probe (w4-m3-probe)))\n    92\t        (w4-log \"W4-M3: thread A foreign call returned t=\" (w4-now)\n    93\t                \" (blocked ~2s from \" t-start \")\")\n    94\t        (thread-join! t-b)\n    95\t        (w4-log \"W4-M3: B-completed-during-A-block probe = \" probe\n    96\t                \" => \" (if (= probe 0)\n    97\t                           \"no callback from B during A's foreign call (callbacks from other Gambit threads are serialized AFTER the foreign call; no released-frame concurrency exists — see W2)