{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_40","type":"agent_message","text":"A configuration-only rebuild does not clear the P2/P3 gate on the source evidence: it may allow another Scheme thread to run, but GC still needs the blocked processor to join its barrier, and foreign-pthread entry still lacks a documented attach/claim protocol. I’ll scope the verdict accordingly and specify the experiment needed to challenge it. P1b also needs a separate dynamic-callback witness: W4 tests static `c-define` callbacks, while the built-in dynamic trampoline generator has no arm64 or x86_64 implementation."}}
